  "recipe": {
    "what": "How a workspace package of this candidate is built. Steps 2 to 5 need the game's own master and the Papyrus compiler on a licensed PC; none of them has been run for this candidate. Nothing is installed, and no licensed file goes into the repository or the cloud.",
    "steps": [
      "1. python3 tools/mercy_briefing_candidate.py verify   (the checkout is this manifest's source)",
      "2. dotnet run --project tools/PluginBuilder -- --out <new folder>/plugin --fallout4-esm <Fallout4.esm>   (self-check must pass; read the report: the new quest, book and nine messages, and the ids below)",
      "3. dotnet run --project tools/WorldSliceBuilder -- <Fallout4.esm> <new folder>/world --story-source <new folder>/plugin/TheLastMeridian.esp --natural --private-shelter-detail   (the same exterior options as the Details package; WorldStory refuses a clone whose walk does not point at the master's TLM_MercyBriefing)",
      "4. Compile all 20 scripts under scripts/Source/User/TLM with the game's Papyrus compiler (tools/win/Build-Scripts.ps1 compiles every .psc there). A fresh compile; no earlier PEX is reused or assumed byte-identical.",
      "5. python3 tools/mercy_briefing_candidate.py measure <bundle folder>   (prints the measured digests for a build receipt; it changes no pin)"
    ],
    "expectedIds": "The eleven records appended to tools/PluginBuilder/formkeys.txt keep their numbers in every build: the allocator reads that file."
  },
